,"@type":"personal","namePart":["Kissinger, Henry,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1923-2023"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Case studies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Case studies."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Études de cas."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2022"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2022"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"London :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Allen Lane, an imprint of Penguin Books,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2022."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xxvi, 499 pages : illustrations ; 24 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"The statesman and diplomat analyses how six extraordinary leaders he has known have shaped their countries and the world Kissinger's six leaders are Konrad Adenauer, Charles de Gaulle, Richard Nixon, Anwar Sadat, Lee Kuan Yew, and Margaret Thatcher. All of them were formed in a period when established institutions collapsed all over Europe, colonial structures gave way to independent states in Asia and Africa, and a new international order had to be created from the vestiges of the old. Kissinger penetratingly analyses each of these leaders' careers through the highly individual strategies of statecraft which he presents them as embodying, to show how it is the combination of character and circumstance which creates history. Kissinger's public experience, personal knowledge and historical perceptions enrich the book with insights and judgements such as only he could make\"--Publisher's description."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Konrad Adenauer: The strategy of humility -- Charles de Gaulle: The strategy of will -- Richard Nixon: The strategy of equilibrium -- Anwar Sadat: The strategy of transcendence -- Lee Kuan Yew: The strategy of excellence -- Margaret Thatcher: The strategy of conviction -- Conclusion: The evolution of leadership."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Henry Kissinger."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Political leadership","genre":"Case studies"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Heads of state","History"],"temporal":"20th century","genre":"Case studies"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Diplomacy","genre":"Case studies"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"World politics","temporal":"1945-1989"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Heads of state","History"],"temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"World politics","temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Chefs d'État","Histoire"],"temporal":"20e siècle"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Politique mondiale","temporal":"20e siècle"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Chefs d'État","Histoire"],"temporal":"20e siècle","genre":"Études de cas"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Diplomatie","genre":"Études de cas"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Politique mondiale","temporal":"1945-1989"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Diplomacy"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Heads of state"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Political leadership"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"World politics"},{"@authority":"nbdbt","topic":"Organisatieleer; alge